  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Amarshiha Ramjilal Yadav vs The State Of Maharashtra on 8 November, 2023 Author: M. S. Karnik Bench: M. S. Karnik 2023:Bhc-As:34254 Darshan Patil 27-ba-3518-23.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Bail Application No. 3518 Of 2023 Amarshiha Ramjilal Yadav ..Applicant Vs. The State Of Maharashtra ..Respondent ------------ Adv. Rajas Naik for the Applicant. Mr. P. H. Gaikwad, App for the State. Psi Amol Chindhe, Manor Poice Station, Palghar. ------------ Coram : M. S. Karnik, J.",
    "facts": "the informant who is a Food and Drug Inspector received secret information that Ashok Leyland vehicle bearing No. MH-55/AB 5033 is standing on the Mumbai-Ahmedabad Highway at Chellar Phata, Manor containing contraband articles. On search of the said vehicle, the muddemal i.e. Pan Masala, Jafrani Jarda, Gutkha and Tobacco total worth Rs.94,16,160/- was found. The contraband has been recovered. The applicant was the driver of the vehicle. The goods did not belong to him. 4. All the other Sections except Section 328 of the IPC are bailable. The issue of whether the purchase, sale or transportation of such contraband is covered by Section 328 of the IPC is pending consideration before the Hon'ble Supreme Court. There are no criminal antecedents reported against the applicant.",
